{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat collab/1793030000000-engineer-8f1c.prompt.md'","aggregated_output":"Created-GMT: 2026-10-15 09:10:00 GMT\nCreated-Local: 2026-10-15 16:10:00 +07\nCoding-Agent: codex\nSession-ID: pending (provider-generated)\n# Task: 8f-1 continue: steps 3, 4a, 5 with one sequencing deferral (uncommitted)\nRole: VM Runtime\nImplementers:\n- Model: gpt-6.1-sol | Assigned: 2026-10-15 16:10 +07 | Status: active | Rationale: continues own slice; the Architect (Fable) confirms the deferral in the final review\n\nWorktree /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-p8f1k already holds your uncommitted steps 0-2 (keep byte-identical). Your BLOCKED report (collab/1792051089473-engineer-8f1b.report.md) was correct: yin.vm/opcode-table and the opcase macro are still read by semantic.cljc, which lives until 8f-3. DECISION (orchestrator, mirrors the Architect's own 4a/4b split principle: a var dies in the slice of its last consumer): in step 3 DO NOT delete yin.vm/opcode-table or opcase from vm.cljc; they move to 8f-3 together with semantic.cljc (record this in your report as a deferral). Do EVERYTHING else in step 3 (delete completion.cljc and completion_test.cljc, vm.cljc segment-extraction-queries/segment-requirements and the ast-requirements docstring sentence, the scan_test/query_test/cell_test/publish_test/debruijn_code_test edits, the two docstrings linker.cljc ~2057 and driver.clj:8), then step 4a (rule_r_test deftest removal, the :push footprint row, scan.cljc:76, scan_test:254 rename, query_test footprint assertion), then step 5 gates. If another symbol turns out to be read by a surviving namespace, defer it the same way and list it; if anything else needs a design decision STOP. Read ./collab/1792050511876-architect-8f1-ruling.report.md again for the exact edits. No commit, no stage, no Node/Dart. Report ./collab/<ms>-engineer-8f1c.report.md (headers, per-step counts, deferral list, delete