{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat collab/1792051089473-engineer-8f1b.report.md; git status --short'","aggregated_output":"Completed-GMT: 2026-10-15 07:58:09 GMT\nCompleted-Local: 2026-10-15 14:58:09 +07\nCoding-Agent: codex\nSession-ID: 01a13e8d-1c26-7143-b3a7-32b9681bccd4\n\n# 8f-1b implementation: BLOCKED before step 3\n\nBranch `srvm-phase8f1`, base `d43afbe3`. Implemented steps 0, 1 and 2, in order, running each step's lane before advancing. All changes are unstaged and uncommitted. Existing untracked collab artifacts were preserved. File deletions used filesystem unlink rather than `git rm`, to honor the prompt's explicit no-stage requirement.\n\n## Blocking Architect decision\n\nSection 2 step 3 / R3 directs deletion of `yin.vm/opcode-table` from `src/cljc/yin/vm.cljc`, while explicitly retaining `src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic.cljc` until 8f-3. That retained namespace directly reads the var at lines 624, 634, 767, 768 and 770. The step 3 lane still requires it. Its presence on disk cannot make it compile after deleting a required var.\n\nConfirmed without changing the worktree: a separate JVM ran\n\n```sh\nclojure -M -e \"(require 'yin.vm) (ns-unmap 'yin.vm 'opcode-table) (require 'yin.vm.semantic)\"\n```\n\nExpected diagnostic, exit 1:\n\n```text\nSyntax error compiling at (yin/vm/semantic.cljc:624:37).\nNo such var: vm/opcode-table\n```\n\nThe ruling supplies no split for this dependency (unlike its explicit 4a/4b split for UCF). A decision is needed on deferring this deletion or changing its retained consumer. Neither was inferred or implemented. Per the prompt, STOPPED before step 3; steps 3, 4a and 5 were not started. No completion deletion, footprint edit, UCF shrink, old-kernel deletion, rename, demo port, or docs edit occurred.\n\n## Per-step results\n\n| Step | Implementation / verification | Tests | Assertions | Failures | Errors |\n|---|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n| 0 | `clojure -M:test -n yin.vm.debruijn-code-test -n yin.vm.debruijn-register-code-test`; exit 0 | 47 | 302 | 0 | 0 |\n| 1 | Literal 23-mnemonic table, private terminators, removed old-code require/helpers, updated code prose, prescribed test rewrite with second testing block unchanged. Six-namespace lane with `-e :slow`; exit 0 | 147 | 7217 | 0 | 0 |\n| 2 direct | Deleted old handoff/checkpoint source files; removed first cell-refusal block + handoff require; removed audit allowlist entry. `clojure -M:test -e :slow -n yin.vm.store-write-audit-test -n yang.python.antlr.int-heap-test`; exit 0 | 4 | 157 | 0 | 0 |\n| 2 UCF | `bb test:sub:clj yin.vm.ucf`; 29 namespaces, 80 s, exit 0 | 593 | 6932 | 0 | 0 |\n| 3 | BLOCKED before edits/lane | — | — | — | — |\n| 4a | Not reached | — | — | — | — |\n| 5 | Not reached; no full JVM quick gate, Node or Dart lane | — | — | — | — |\n\nThe UCF wrapper printed a shutdown-hook `Operation not permitted (sysctl failed)` exception after reporting its lane pass. Both wrapper process and test lane exited 0. No loopback/head-board failure occurred in the lanes actually run; the full quick tier that includes that test was not reached.\n\nLint: bare `clj -M:kondo` prints usage, so that alone is not a lint result. Explicit `--lint` over HEAD copies of the six affected files gave 0 errors / 0 warnings; explicit `--lint` over the four surviving modified files gave 0 errors / 0 warnings, exit 0. `git diff --check` passed. No new lint warnings in the touched files. Full-repository step 5 lint was not reached.\n\n## Pinned identities before / after\n\nThe descriptor test form and full golden-expected fixture were compared byte-for-byte to their step 0 copies after all edits; identical. The register test file is wholly byte-identical. No literal was changed.\n\n| Pin | Before | After |\n|---|---|---|\n| `descriptor-declares-the-contract` | `7b7c6ae92e5fe53577718b615a3ed0bdd81796bf8074efe8c07d7005c45f3489` | identical |\n| `golden-descriptor-hash-test` | `aa757659a28f9787e44cd04d02d9f4412eba1088d46a1b07adf9fa820d07e74c` | identical |\n| const-long H | `fa643897ef8a5377b4db7682ec9118149e7c4c01d6b3a1491c4bbe8fe60fd2ba` | identical |\n| const-string H | `d748b428803c06b957fb945df2ca2627633fc8e1cdde0caadb1e90df6f19c5d3` | identical |\n| closure-bound H | `64afffdc1e88fe97911cfac010b98c5f147123942486b947f60c66d20a03f6d7` | identical |\n| load-free H | `9ab244f27567aa96519d602c3555c85bbf283489e8c5d919f70976c3a42e8c63` | identical |\n\nAll four golden `[bytes H]` pairs, exactly as before and after:\n\n```clojure\n{:const-long [\"0302000000102a000000000000000f\"\n                \"fa643897ef8a5377b4db7682ec9118149e7c4c01d6b3a1491c4bbe8fe60fd2ba\"]\n   :const-string [\"030700000005hello0f\"\n                  \"d748b428803c06b957fb945df2ca2627633fc8e1cdde0caadb1e90df6f19c5d3\"]\n   :closure-bound [(str \"02010000000000000002000000000000000f0a0000000000\"\n                        \"00000000000000000000000f\")\n                   \"64afffdc1e88fe97911cfac010b98c5f147123942486b947f60c66d20a03f6d7\"]\n   :load-free [\"0b090000001500000000000700000001x0f\"\n               \"9ab244f27567aa96519d602c3555c85bbf283489e8c5d919f70976c3a42e8c63\"]})\n```\n\n## Deleted-test ledger\n\nCounts distinguish the ruling's intended full slice from the work actually completed.\n\n| Location | Ruling's deletion count | Actually deleted | Replacement / retained fact |\n|---|---:|---:|---|\n| handoff/checkpoint | 0 deftests (already gone in 8d) | 0 | Rows transport tests retained; 593 UCF tests passed. Source deletion only. |\n| completion_test | 19 | 0; step 3 blocked | Intended: scan/assert-agreement + goldens for free names and requirements; engine/lift-slice cell refusals; load_paths + mint for round trip; inline FFI pair set; module discovery and old address-reuse performance facts dropped per R3. All original tests still present. |\n| rule_r_test | 1 | 0; 4a not reached | Intended stamp-verification register-loader port in 8f-3. Existing test retained. |\n| scan_test | 1 | 0; step 3 blocked | Intended deletion of old completion address-reuse performance test; scanner agreement retained. |\n| cell_test | 1 | 0; step 3 blocked | Intended surviving `lift-of-a-bare-cell-ref-is-refused-test`; original completion test retained. |\n| query_test | 1 | 0; step 3 blocked | Intended scanner requirement-agreement coverage; original test retained. |\n| publish_test | 0 deleted, 1 narrowed | 0 deleted, 0 narrowed | Intended manifest-footprint assertion; current completion half retained. |\n| int_heap_test | 0 deftests, first cell-refusal run-all block removed | 0 deftests, block removed | Remaining engine/lift-slice blocks retained. Whole cell-refusal deftest remains slow and was excluded by required quick lane. |\n| debruijn_code_test | 0, one rewritten | 0, one rewritten | Dimension-owned shape/kind assertions, unchanged descriptor and golden pins. |\n\nDeftest source-form occurrences across `test/**/*.{clj,cljc,cljs,cljd}`, matching `\\(deftest\\s` (includes metadata-prefixed test names): **4440 before / 4440 after**, delta 0. No deftest was deleted in completed steps.\n\nLogs: `/tmp/8f1b/step0.log`, `step1.log`, `step2-direct.log`, `step2-ucf.log`, `kondo-before.log`, `kondo-baseline-files.log`, `kondo-after-files.log`, `step3-blocker-proof.log`. UCF test details also in `target/profile/sub-clj.log`.\n\nBLOCKED\n M src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_code.cljc\n D src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/checkpoint.cljc\n D src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/handoff.cljc\n M test/yang/python/antlr/int_heap_test.cljc\n M test/yin/vm/debruijn_code_test.cljc\n M test/yin/vm/store_write_audit_test.clj\n?? collab/1792050170602-engineer-8f1.report.md\n?? collab/1792050511876-architect-8f1-ruling.report.md\n?? collab/1792051089473-engineer-8f1b.report.md\n?? collab/1792560000000-architect-phase8-plan.report.md\n?? collab/1793000000000-engineer-8f1.gpt-6.1-sol.stdout.log\n?? collab/1793000000000-engineer-8f1.prompt.md\n?? collab/1793010000000-architect-8f1-ruling.fable.stdout.log\n??